// ============================================================================
//  v1.89.2 - THE TWO ATTACHMENTS THE PACK-A-PUNCHED WEAPONS CRASHED WITHOUT
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Firing a Pack-a-Punched ported weapon froze the game hard - no GSC error,
//  the console log simply ended mid-line. The upgraded defs are the only half
//  of each pair that carries an `attachments` field, which is why the base
//  weapon fired fine and only the upgraded one died.
//
//  Of the 8 attachments those defs name, six were already in mod.ff as
//  dependencies. These two were not:
//      holo            <- qbb95_upgraded_zm
//      steadyaim_smg   <- vector_upgraded_zm, vector_extclip_upgraded_zm
//  steadyaim_smg is the Vector's, which is the weapon the user froze on.
//
//  🛑 ,defaultattachment IS NOT MISSING and must not be added here - it is
//  already declared at mod_base.zone:476. Its real asset name carries a LEADING
//  COMMA (the Unlinker prints it as `attachment, ,defaultattachment`), so a
//  naive lookup for "defaultattachment" reports a false absence. That false
//  positive cost one wrong diagnosis; check the raw listing, not a built key.
// ============================================================================
attachment,holo
attachment,steadyaim_smg

// ============================================================================
//  v1.89.3 - THE PACK-A-PUNCH ATTACHMENT TABLE, UNDER A MOD-PRIVATE NAME
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  _zm_weapons::add_attachments() looks the UPGRADED weapon name up in
//  `zm/pap_attach.csv` and assigns level.zombie_weapons[w].default_attachment
//  from column 1. Every stock Pack-a-Punched weapon has a row there; none of
//  the nine ported ones did - so a packed weapon was built with an attachment
//  set its def requires and nothing supplied. That is the crash on firing.
//
//  🛑 THE STOCK TABLE CANNOT BE OVERRIDDEN. `zm/pap_attach.csv` is owned by
//  patch_zm.ff; declaring that exact name here makes mod.ff the owner, mod.ff
//  loads first, and the owning zone then dies with
//      COM_ERROR Attempting to override asset ... from zone 'mod'
//  which is the same shape that made Origins unbootable in v1.19.0.
//
//  🌟 SO IT SHIPS UNDER A NEW NAME AND IS SELECTED IN SCRIPT.
//  _zm_weapons.gsc:582 reads `if ( isdefined( level.weapon_attachment_table ) )
//  table = level.weapon_attachment_table;` - a hook Treyarch left open. The
//  file carries ALL 29 stock rows verbatim plus 7 of ours, so pointing the
//  whole game at it changes nothing for any stock weapon.
// ============================================================================
stringtable,zm/pap_attach_qol.csv

// ============================================================================
//  v1.89.5 - THE 13 ATTACHMENTUNIQUES, AS FASTFILE ASSETS THIS TIME
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  🛑 THE ACTUAL CAUSE OF THE PACK-A-PUNCH CRASH, MEASURED IN THE RUNTIME LOG.
//  console_zm.log prints, once per weapon, at map load:
//      Couldn't find attachmentunique 'au_mp7_dualclip'
//      Couldn't find attachmentunique 'au_mp7_none'
//      ... 13 lines, EXACTLY the 13 the nine upgraded defs name, and ZERO
//      lines for any of the 89 stock au_* the mod already ships.
//  The upgraded def is the only half of each pair with an `attachmentUniques`
//  field, so a Pack-a-Punched weapon is built pointing at a record that does
//  not exist, and the first shot dereferences it: 0xC0000005.
//
//  🛑 WHY v1.89.1 DID NOT FIX THIS. It put all 13 in the raw `attachmentunique\`
//  folder and confirmed them inside the deployed mod.iwd - both true, and
//  irrelevant. RAW IS NOT THE DELIVERY PATH FOR THIS ASSET TYPE. All 13 are
//  verified present in the deployed mod.iwd and the engine still cannot find
//  them. The 89 that work are FASTFILE assets: mod_base.zone declares 91
//  `attachmentunique,` lines and mod_locations.zone declared none. The raw
//  folder is what the Linker was fed from, not what the game reads.
//
//  Resolvable with no new --load: all 13 are in common_mp.ff, and the three
//  peacekeeper ones in common_patch_mp.ff - both already loaded, last, for the
//  weapon port. No zombies fastfile owns any of these names (checked against
//  common_zm, patch_zm, zm_transit, zm_tomb, zm_buried: 0 matches), so mod.ff
//  owning them cannot re-own anything.
// ============================================================================
attachmentunique,au_mp7_none
attachmentunique,au_mp7_dualclip
attachmentunique,au_vector_none
attachmentunique,au_vector_steadyaim
attachmentunique,au_sig556_none
attachmentunique,au_sig556_gl
attachmentunique,au_sa58_none
attachmentunique,au_sa58_sf
attachmentunique,au_qbb95_none
attachmentunique,au_qbb95_holo
attachmentunique,au_peacekeeper_none
attachmentunique,au_peacekeeper_grip
attachmentunique,au_peacekeeper_reflex
